            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 11</span><h1>Dataflow with TPL Dataflow</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>35 min</span><span class="lesson-level intermediate">Intermediate</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>What is TPL Dataflow?</h2>
                    <p>TPL Dataflow provides building blocks for creating producer-consumer pipelines with built-in buffering, throttling, and parallelism.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash">dotnet add package System.Threading.Tasks.Dataflow</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Basic Blocks</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// TransformBlock - transforms input to output
var transformBlock = new TransformBlock&lt;string, int&gt;(
    s =&gt; s.Length,
    new ExecutionDataflowBlockOptions { MaxDegreeOfParallelism = 4 });

// ActionBlock - performs action on input (no output)
var actionBlock = new ActionBlock&lt;int&gt;(
    n =&gt; Console.WriteLine($"Length: {n}"));

// BufferBlock - simple buffer/queue
var bufferBlock = new BufferBlock&lt;string&gt;();</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Building a Pipeline</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Create blocks
var downloadBlock = new TransformBlock&lt;string, string&gt;(
    async url =&gt; await httpClient.GetStringAsync(url),
    new ExecutionDataflowBlockOptions { MaxDegreeOfParallelism = 5 });

var parseBlock = new TransformBlock&lt;string, Document&gt;(
    html =&gt; ParseHtml(html),
    new ExecutionDataflowBlockOptions { MaxDegreeOfParallelism = 10 });

var saveBlock = new ActionBlock&lt;Document&gt;(
    async doc =&gt; await SaveDocumentAsync(doc));

// Link blocks together
var linkOptions = new DataflowLinkOptions { PropagateCompletion = true };
downloadBlock.LinkTo(parseBlock, linkOptions);
parseBlock.LinkTo(saveBlock, linkOptions);

// Feed data
foreach (var url in urls)
    await downloadBlock.SendAsync(url);

// Signal completion and wait
downloadBlock.Complete();
await saveBlock.Completion;</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Bounded Capacity</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Limit memory usage with bounded capacity
var options = new ExecutionDataflowBlockOptions
{
    BoundedCapacity = 100,  // Max 100 items in queue
    MaxDegreeOfParallelism = 4
};

var block = new TransformBlock&lt;Input, Output&gt;(Process, options);

// SendAsync will wait if buffer is full
await block.SendAsync(item);</code></pre>
                </section>

